+# Mira accessories: read-only baseline and micro-part handoff
+
+Latest instruction changed the method before new accessory source was written: first generate parts small enough to construct individually in a short step, fix their common interfaces, then assemble the whole character. No hand, boot, staff, IK helper or integration patch was implemented in this unit. The dedicated checkout remains based on `fc311bac0134b58e04891264c405bfd61eba22e3`; runtime, package/lock, actor, shared geometry and references are unchanged. No browser, remote, server, generation or external service operation was made by this author. `npm ci` completed using the existing lockfile.
+
+The three original reference PNGs were inspected with view_image. Their hashes and paths are in references.json. The existing shoe body is a reshaped sphere, with a separate flattened sphere sole; the reference additionally resolves heel, welt, vamp and wrapped shaft. The five-finger bone layout is present, but reference grasp conformity is not established. The staff reference resolves wood, crossed grip leather, foot ferrule, a three-dimensional oval cage, a pale core and a small round finial. These are design observations, not calibrated dimensions or proof of rendered quality.
+
+`baseline.mjs` executes the real Three native geometry and actor API without a renderer. It requires the base actor and detailed-geometry bytes exactly, reads the original geometry from Git, exposes private constructors only in an in-memory bundle, and edits no source. Re-run from this checkout root with `node docs/evidence/mira-accessories-v60/baseline.mjs`; it writes JSON only to stdout. The first exploratory invocation had a relative import-path typo and failed before model evaluation; the corrected and saved oracle is the successful path. No model repair is hidden in the oracle.
+
+## Actual baseline
+
+- NPC: 6,718 triangles, 13 meshes, 5,030 vertices, 41 unique bones. These are source geometry counts, not measured rendered draw calls or device cost.
+- Shoe upper: 286 × 158 × 111 mm; sole: 286 × 158 × 20 mm. Sole bottom is foot-local −108 mm. Upper min Y −87 mm versus sole max Y −88 mm establishes a 1 mm separation between their vertical bounds; no identical-footprint nearest-distance claim is made. Each original shoe component is closed after position welding at 1e−7 m, with zero degenerate/nonmanifold faces in this finite check.
+- Original right-coded hand-1 has 265 vertices / 380 triangles excluding staff. Staff shaft diameter is 52 mm and length 1,490 mm; original combined prop extends −790 to +911.05 mm locally, total 1,701.05 mm.
+- The original oval ring is 201.81 × 282.10 × 15.04 mm, so its depth is much thinner than the resolved cage in the part reference.
+- Actual idle at t=0/1/3 s places the original hand-1 at about y=.823 m. Staff tilt is 28.23–28.58 degrees from world vertical and the lower endpoint is 126.79–130.37 mm above the flat ground.
+- Within the selected 265 right-hand skin vertices, 63 are radially inside the old 26 mm-radius shaft, maximum radial vertex penetration 23.57 mm. This finite vertex/cylinder diagnostic is not a full triangle intersection test or a claim that all contact is erroneous.
+
+These old cases deliberately retain hand-1. The parent subsequently confirmed the fixed FRONT reference puts the staff on the character's anatomical right, meaning **hand-0 / actor −X / front image left**. The future candidate must use that side; this record does not rewrite the baseline to hide its handedness difference. No reference image was mirrored.
+
+## Micro-part handoff
+
+STAFF_MICRO_BOM.json and .md are byte copies of the external planning handoff in q-character-reference-v60/micro-part-planning/accessories. The first 16-ID plan omitted the two bronze grip-end collars visible in the original close reference. The corrected plan defines S01–S18, 19 physical pieces because S05 consists of two opposite strips. S17/S18 are the separate lower/upper grip collars; S06 remains the lantern neck socket. Each has a frame, dimensions, interface and simple construction method. These are explicit authored registration values against the old approximately 1.7 m prop, not dimensions extracted from generated pictures.
+
+S15 follows the round finial visible in the close reference; an unverified hanging loop is excluded. The obscured back cage rib and hidden seats are stated construction assumptions. The two glass poles meet their named lower cup and upper cap seats; no unspecified floating connector is treated as resolved. Hand-to-staff pose is still unimplemented and must be settled after the complete micro references are fixed. Boot and hand micro-part tables were not expanded because the parent prioritized the first staff image trial.
+
+Only evidence/planning is being committed. No new micro image, new 3D part, pose repair, build result, WebGL picture, artistic acceptance or PS4-quality completion is claimed. Parent-supervised context creation failed before drawing; its actual diagnostic lives in the viewer record. All accepted tools are complete, active sessions 0.
